\"node is not a voter\")\n    45\t\n    46\t\t// ErrLeadershipLost is returned when a leader fails to commit a log entry\n    47\t\t// because it's been deposed in the process.\n    48\t\tErrLeadershipLost = errors.New(\"leadership lost while committing log\")\n    49\t\n    50\t\t// ErrAbortedByRestore is returned when a leader fails to commit a log\n    51\t\t// entry because it's been superseded by a user snapshot restore.\n    52\t\tErrAbortedByRestore = errors.New(\"snapshot restored while committing log\")\n    53\t\n    54\t\t// ErrRaftShutdown is returned when operations are requested against an\n    55\t\t// inactive Raft.\n    56\t\tErrRaftShutdown = errors.New(\"raft is already shutdown\")\n    57\t\n    58\t\t// ErrEnqueueTimeout is returned when a command fails due to a timeout.\n    59\t\tErrEnqueueTimeout = errors.New(\"timed out enqueuing operation\")\n    60\t\n    61\t\t// ErrNothingNewToSnapshot is returned when trying to create a snapshot\n    62\t\t// but there's nothing new committed to the FSM since we started.\n    63\t\tErrNothingNewToSnapshot = errors.New(\"nothing new to snapshot\")\n    64\t\n    65\t\t// ErrUnsupportedProtocol is returned when an operation is attempted\n    66\t\t// that's not supported by the current protocol version.\n    67\t\tErrUnsupportedProtocol = errors.New(\"operation not supported with current protocol version\")\n    68\t\n    69\t\t// ErrCantBootstrap is returned when attempt is made to bootstrap a\n    70\t\t// cluster that already has state present.\n    71\t\tErrCantBootstrap = errors.New(\"bootstrap only works on new clusters\")\n    72\t\n    73\t\t// ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress is returned when the leader is rejecting\n    74\t\t// client requests because it is attempting to transfer leadership.\n    75\t\tErrLeadershipTransferInProgress = errors.New(\"leadership transfer in progress\")\n    76\t\n    77\t\t// ErrIncompatibleLogStore is returned when the log store does not support\n    78\t\t// or implement some required methods.\n    79\t\tErrIncompatibleLogStore = errors.New(\"log store does not implement some required methods or malformed\")\n    80\t)\n    81\t\n    82\t// Raft implements a Raft node.\n    83\ttype Raft struct {\n    84\t\traftState\n    85\t\n    86\t\t// protocolVersion is used to inter-operate with Raft servers running\n    87\t\t// different versions of the library. See comments in config.go for more\n    88\t\t// details.\n    89\t\tprotocolVersion ProtocolVersion\n    90\t\n    91\t\t// applyCh is used to async send logs to the main thread to\n    92\t\t// be committed and applied to the FSM.\n    93\t\tapplyCh chan *logFuture\n    94\t\n    95\t\t// conf stores the current configuration to use. This is the most recent one\n    96\t\t// provided. All reads of config values should use the config() helper method\n    97\t\t// to read this safely.\n    98\t\tconf atomic.Value\n    99\t\n   100\t\t// confReloadMu ensures that only one thread can reload config at once since\n   101\t\t// we need to read-modify-write the atomic. It is NOT necessary to hold this\n   102\t\t// for any other operation e.g. reading config using config().\n   103\t\tconfReloadMu sync.Mutex\n   104\t\n   105\t\t// FSM is the client state machine to apply commands to\n   106\t\tfsm FSM\n   107\t\n   108\t\t// fsmMutateCh is used to send state-changing updates to the FSM. This\n   109\t\t// receives pointers to commitTuple structures when applying logs or\n   110\t\t// pointers to restoreFuture structures when restoring a snapshot. We\n   111\t\t// need control over the order of these operations when doing user\n   112\t\t// restores so that we finish applying any old log applies before we\n   113\t\t// take a user snapshot on the leader, otherwise we might restore the\n   114\t\t// snapshot and apply old logs to it that were in the pipe.\n   115\t\tfsmMutateCh chan interface{}\n   116\t\n   117\t\t// fsmSnapshotCh is used to trigger a new snapshot being taken\n  